   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "The quotient of consecutive terms is \\( r = - \\frac{x^{2}}{7} \\), the same for every n, so the series is geometric. Its first term is the \\( n = 2 \\) term, \\( a = \\frac{5 x^{4}}{49} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Multiply",
            [
               "Rational",
               5,
               49
            ],
            [
               "Power",
               "x",
               4
            ]
         ],
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99067",
         "rule_named": "first term and ratio"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "It converges when \\( |r| < 1 \\), that is for \\( \\left|x\\right| < \\sqrt{7} \\).",
         "rule_named": "convergence condition"
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "There the sum is \\( \\frac{a}{1 - r} = \\frac{5 x^{4}}{7 \\left(x^{2} + 7\\right)} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
